(7661550, 1248267, 141319, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by glad2badad:</b></div><hr/><i> Personally, I preferred seeing entries where the photographer had to go find a reflection (a window, a still body of water, etc.).  Using a mirror just seems, I don''t know, too easy and convenient - the easy way out I guess.  Not to say studio work is easy, just different.  I was one of your under 5 scores. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you, I really appreciate your comment. We obviously disagree ;-), but that''s OK. Thanks for explaining your score. <br/> <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by glad2badad: Personally, I preferred seeing entries where the photographer had to go find a reflection (a window, a still body of water, etc.).  Using a mirror just seems, I don''t know, too easy and convenient - the easy way out I guess.  Not to say studio work is easy, just different.  I was one of your under 5 scores.   Thank you, I really appreciate your comment. We obviously disagree ;-), but that''s OK. Thanks for explaining your score.  ', '2020-05-06 14:39:48.000000', NULL, 0),
